entical outputs even if they’re statistically independent. The user is pushing for independently running these models to assess the known structure against the uncertainty of outputs. I'll be careful in my analysis here!**Considering decision frameworks**\n\nI shouldn't just assume that independent randomness filters out shared reasoning since I don't know the output in advance. I'm thinking about how cooperation plays into this—can I confidently cooperate? Evaluating causal decision theory (CDT) versus evidential decision theory (EDT) might help, especially about the prisoner's dilemma. It's interesting that they emphasize different methods to avoid similar output correlations. I want to make sure I'm using EDT rather than relying on altruism. In the end, I'll choose to pass based on strong evidence and shared reasoning. Let's wrap this up!","format":"openai-responses-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABq8PqMp_RNe_MKfe35iCTlHKO_x86cKrsLmXMqlpva4V1olkV7x--R-y91b6-kb8jiReXohRE7F-2F7ITrw_qYpO9mxV06c_vKWwxwru50sgELE9-eMkL0mrYsh63PtOpi4cAE4J7VwBnKYtwexCzbSLfB8B2mi6hRIpUyApV2JNUKu0bl0AT7YXGDy354v67iKX8MHD5pXAbF-Jy83Gu8k6ZfXPXZia5hc1SraTbOm_7p_X0_Tm8lCIfq3OsaL4JI8IxFUTar7ie_mfFTCR7sIoR0anyz-i3NqIcpB7v4M27R19Ak3Y-aTp4bBd3A99HiDrkk_GJZaZ9urx7uJE5y9M2iEJIlhjJ5EDFo6xh4Yw4l4v_uQoZ9NkjW34CCBHEGcNDM-rWjWOkzFEoNMAyL6GEfzvrWUqv_gRw0gJpMoR9kfk5YkXRnbGmFJvMT8w5e2w95MG577sPnx1hIvNiFdwgXDOQgiu_75ty8RLFJxUnsf2gM-RUFgJWgCGruemvXCd-6E8oEGuiY1XnMqrrd3Ho4W5ywwAyFL3wzXKtATo9RWJ31Zfgn8I7iHfewHGxmvMZrmseuSNdfv75QG0wjJDTIxxQTNZ0O06BlHAELWj6fy98dDmItU4afa8-03Zn57BWzDi8WFJ-fGSTFq0cbZVMunkyjIwo4PR22qvJ-L5sEgnl8yB8gsG3n5i-CAMrdhO2hp5w5YRS-IFaHodM6G8L8Ngqk_dv9Sr27gHpOPOmJWND112164WTwKcngEenD2CMEX50ltT-IycTX1CUHcERDOjYw8FzyizRmykcwZ86nUJPWHlxieH75euJOtFGSUGXAPNnDhSYzr9iBoEAsgMmH5pQg4bTpxN3cxv5jI1P0bVVUMOaDutMbulsYEdoPXzGVHLGT86C_xZMFzG-aCi-Eo7SKzRZe5RJBibc5a20WCxG5A7jvtMJnAOuFGBNNjn8n5ODSzJeAyxYFTPHK7ToQNvkSillYOhPhIPR8wNIvjttcUXgq5D5oy8WxxNzxQBCIfVeYCnTqogrxuVCDve54mWtsJZ8LX